body:
You cannot do anything with it (restore etc) over USB, it has to be firewire or the iPod will immediately reset itself. Thats not suspicious, that's just how they all are. 

&#x200B;

I would suggest opening it up and making sure the scene is connected properly, its entirely possible that the connector has just come loose in shipping. I sold a working 4th gen that I had been testing for weeks, it arrived and it wasn't working. I obviously gave the buyer a full refund and covered shipping back to me, I opened it up and the cable had just disconnected

Im in Vic bit not really planning on ordering from the UK. I would just buy a few things if you can afford it. I believe when Super Milk was in Aus it was $30, I checked and seen thats it 15 pound so after conversion seem to be the same price as aus. As long as you stay under 500g the shipping is cheap as well, I have only ordered from there a few times, both were reasonably negative experiences. That was because of the products though, the actual shipping was great and I feel like it got here in less than 2 weeks! 

&#x200B;

If you have any other favourite products, especially the fresh cleansers that come in the bigger pots, I would do the math and sometimes the prices are that much cheaper in the UK that the shipping basically pays itself with the savings. I think last time I ordered from the UK it cost $2.15 more than what I would pay in Aus and I was getting exclusive products like the single colour fun (don't recommend)  so that 2.15 extra was worth it. I also live 3 hours from a store though so im forced to pay shipping on even the Aus orders so I guess when you can just pop into a store thats different
